        "original_id": "a5e96653-deef-5db8-aca9-c54f621f464a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: G. D. Spradlin, Marlon Brando, Pat Hingle\n- Works: On the Waterfront, The Godfather, A Streetcar Named Desire, Viva Zapata!, Sayonara\n- Topics: Film and television credits, acting roles, co-stars\n\nFacts:\n- In 1951, Marlon Brando appeared in A Streetcar Named Desire.\n- In 1954, Marlon Brando won an Academy Award for playing Terry Malloy in On the Waterfront.\n- In 1954, On the Waterfront was Pat Hingle's first film.\n- In 1957, Sayonara was released as a Technicolor American film starring Marlon Brando and presented in Technirama.\n- In 1972, Marlon Brando won an Academy Award for playing Vito Corleone in The Godfather.\n- Marlon Brando also appeared in Viva Zapata!.\n- G. D. Spradlin was credited in more than 70 television and film productions.\n- G. D. Spradlin performed alongside actors including Marlon Brando, Al Pacino, Charlton Heston, George C. Scott, and Johnny Depp.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
